# SELinux contexts for the com.matonos.flatpak APEX.
#
# Patterns are relative to the APEX mount point (/apex/com.matonos.flatpak);
# the leading "/" is the apex image root, exactly as e2fsdroid/apexd apply
# them. Everything not matched explicitly stays system_file/system_file_type,
# which is what the moved binaries and NDK libraries used in system_ext before.
#
# The exec types below are IDENTICAL to the ones the same binaries carried at
# /system_ext/... today. No new SELinux types or allows are introduced by the
# move: the domains/transitions in
# systembridge/sepolicy/system_ext/private/matonos_system_bridge.te are
# unchanged. The plain `flatpak` launcher and `flatpak-portal` keep
# system_file, as today; only the Flatpak CLI had its own exec type.
(/.*)?                       u:object_r:system_file:s0
/bin/bwrap                   u:object_r:matonos_bwrap_exec:s0
/bin/matonos-bwrap           u:object_r:matonos_bwrap_exec:s0
/bin/matonos-app-exec        u:object_r:matonos_app_exec_exec:s0
/bin/matonos-mount-helper    u:object_r:matonos_mount_helper_exec:s0
/bin/matonos-flatpak         u:object_r:matonos_flatpak_cli_exec:s0
/bin/matonos-flatpak-store   u:object_r:matonos_flatpak_installer_exec:s0